preConditionHook:
// Brooks's gap-open discipline: do not chase the open. The session gapped
// above the prior day's high extreme, an early pullback has already retraced
// at least gapFillFraction of the way back into the gap, and this bar resumes
// away from the prior day's range -- a bull bar closing above the previous
// bar's high. Short is the mirror below the prior day's low.
//
// curOpen / curHigh / curLow ARE OpenD(0) / HighD(0) / LowD(0), and prevHigh
// / prevLow ARE HighD(1) / LowD(1), which the twin calls and the engine does
// not expose. MEASURED (the highd/lowd register row): the day is the
// wall-clock CALENDAR date, the SAME boundary as date <> date[1]; xxxD(0) is
// the running value INCLUSIVE of the current bar and OpenD(0) is the date's
// first bar open; the prior-day forms return a -1 SENTINEL while fewer than
// that many complete days exist. Because HighD(0)/LowD(0) already mean 'since
// the session open', the merged pseudocode's lowest(low, barsIntoSession)
// needs no bars-into-session counter here.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the session starts at the
// wall-clock close-date change, day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)),
// where the running values roll.
//
// WARM-UP, the one place the twins can differ, exactly as in
// FailedBreakoutOfPriorSessionExtreme: TradeStation's HighD reads the chart's
// own data and answers on the first evaluated bar, while this mirror sees
// only bars from Max Bars Back on. sawStart makes that honest -- a day
// becomes 'the prior session' only once its own first bar has been observed,
// so prevHigh / prevLow hold the -1 sentinel through the first partial day
// and the first fully observed day, the rule is silent there, and the two
// twins agree exactly from the second date change on. The same guard also
// covers curOpen, which is 0.0 until the first observed date change.
//
// The retracement test is a MULTIPLICATION of the gap height, not a ratio: EL
// raises a runtime divide-by-zero and a zero-height gap is legal data.
//
// gapFillFraction IS INVENTED -- the book gives no depth for the pullback --
// so it is an input at 0.5 rather than a hard-coded number. The book also
// gates the setup on a DAILY buy/sell setup being in force; that
// higher-timeframe flag is DROPPED rather than inherited, the engine being
// single-timeframe.
//
// Kept apart from SessionGapFirstBarReversalEntry (the session's very first
// bar only, and a reversal bar) and from FailedBreakoutOfPriorSessionExtreme
// (any bar that pierces and recovers the level, no gap and no retracement
// term). Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    if (sawStart) {
        prevHigh = curHigh;
        prevLow = curLow;
    }
    sawStart = true;
    curOpen = open[0];
    curHigh = high[0];
    curLow = low[0];
} else {
    if (el_gt(high[0], curHigh)) curHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], curLow)) curLow = low[0];
}
longSig = !el_eq(prevHigh, -1.0) && el_gt(curOpen, prevHigh)
    && el_le(curLow, curOpen - gapFillFraction * (curOpen - prevHigh))
    && el_gt(close[0], open[0]) && el_gt(close[0], high[1]);
shortSig = !el_eq(prevLow, -1.0) && el_lt(curOpen, prevLow)
    && el_ge(curHigh, curOpen + gapFillFraction * (prevLow - curOpen))
    && el_lt(close[0], open[0]) && el_lt(close[0], low[1]);
